From bddc002ed5b6a57766823640bd9bae780112cc33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:20:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1018/1198] Keys: move the score, catch a style naming another
 key; adapter rows line up
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HERESY 1018.
- heresy-transpose.js moves an ABC score to any key: every note by the same
  semitones and a fixed number of letters, against both key signatures and
  the accidentals that last to the end of a bar; chord symbols move too;
  headers, inline fields, comments and decorations are left alone; it checks
  every note it moved. Majors, minors and the church modes; nearest, up or
  down. Checked against the Python transposer of the B♭ minor experiment:
  the same bytes, and D minor -> B♭ minor -> D minor returns the original.
- The score drawer shows the score's key and moves it.
- Under the style: when the style names a key and the score is in another,
  a warning ("the song follows the score") with "Move the score to …" and
  "Write … in the style". Plans, Retakes and opened prompts are checked too.
  Measured on 30.09.2026: a style agreeing with its score sang clearer.
- Adapter rows have one shape: the name with its trigger word small under it
  (or "✓ in style"), the sliders of the halves it has, remove. Since a row
  lost its unused slider (1016) the old five-column grid had drifted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
